      "text_raw": "For common-mode opera-\ntion, the common-mode\ninput voltage sees a load\ncapacitance C , which is\nINCM\na lot larger.\nThe feedback capacitors\nC and also the sampling\nF\ncapacitors C are all\nS\ndoubled.\nThe CMFB amplifier has\nto drive larger load capaci-\ntances than the differential\none. Moreover, it is always\nconnected in unity gain, for\nwhich stability is harder to\nachieve. These are two\nreasons for trying to reduce the power consumption as much as possible.",
      "text": "For common-mode operation, the common-mode input voltage sees a load capacitance C , which is INCM a lot larger. The feedback capacitors C and also the sampling F capacitors C are all S doubled. The CMFB amplifier has to drive larger load capacitances than the differential one. Moreover, it is always connected in unity gain, for which stability is harder to achieve. These are two reasons for trying to reduce the power consumption as much as possible."
